  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Integrated public dense vectors over ZZ and QQ with canonical generated FmpzVector/FmpqVector resources. Construction, mutation, same-base arithmetic, scalar products, equality, and independent shallow/deep copies stay on the resource; exact matrix-vector results are adopted without materializing a host element list. Adopted resources validate dimensions and close on mismatch. Slicing is currently one documented bulk host-materialization boundary rather than N scalar foreign calls. Independent review approved the explicit list-free but non-zero-copy ByteRegion matrix bridge, lifecycle behavior, and follow-up ABI debt. The consolidated branch passes focused public and sanitizer tests plus its 100000-entry resource benchmark.",
    "risks": [
      "The current exact matrix-vector ABI exchanges a canonical ByteRegion: input serializes and reparses the vector, while output serializes a temporary FLINT result and parses/copies it into the public resource. No host element list is constructed, but this is not zero-copy.",
      "Exact slicing bulk-materializes and re-imports once, and mixed ZZ/QQ arithmetic currently materializes during FmpzVector-to-FmpqVector conversion; neither path has a direct generated resource declaration yet.",
      "This lane deliberately overlaps src/baselib/matrix.py with its declared qq-sparse-random dependency and must be integrated after that lane."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Add direct FmpzVector/FmpqVector matrix-vector declarations to remove the remaining canonical-byte copy.",
      "Add generated exact-vector slicing and FmpzVector-to-FmpqVector conversion declarations to remove the remaining host-list boundaries.",
      "Register exact_vector_public.py in pyrightconfig.json through the shared integration lane.",
      "Extend resource-backed bulk publication to exact matrix rows, columns, and diagonals when profiling justifies it."
    ]
  }
